                        "review": "This game has had a really long development cycle. \nI've been waiting since twenty-seventeen, and I'm glad I have something like this to fill my time with (especially now, given the bizarre circumstances many of us are in). Was it worth the wait? I mean, for someone who's been hanging around for this long, I think I'm just glad that it's finally here-- so I'd say, \"Yeah.\" \n\nBut I'm also biased. \n\nIt's a simplistic runner with character customization, numerous death screens (as well as a hyper-aware loading screen), gore, and crude humor, meaning this leads to an overall very enjoyable experience. Well, it's enjoyable if you don't mind dying a lot. There's also some random lag that pops up occasionally, which can destroy a near-perfect run-- and I'm sure this will be fixed in a future update. Other than that, I'm very happy with this product. \nIt is worth five bucks, without a doubt. \n\nI only hope the developer considers adding more levels and bosses...and maybe a few more enemies.",
